tion 4","- Last iteration summary: Selected T2: Testify automatic rollback on failure | Execution: succeeded | Verification: failed | Outcome: partial_progress | Backlog remaining: 5"],"taskPlanContext":["## Task Plan","- Reasoning: This task closes a data-integrity gap in Testify: once POST succeeds, any later PATCH or CE-verification failure currently risks leaving orphaned FO records and stale cached instance URLs behind. The key challenge is to add rollback only for freshly created records, treat DELETE 404 as a successful no-op during cleanup, and prove the behavior with focused tests around failure paths and persisted configuration state.","- Approach: Add a best-effort rollback path around the Testify run flow that deletes newly created records on downstream failure, clears persisted instance metadata, and expands cleanup handling/tests to treat already-missing records as success.","- Steps: Inspect the Testify execution path in `plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/DualWriteMapBrowserViewModel.Testify.cs` and identify the exact points where a successful POST transitions into PATCH and CE-verification so rollback can be triggered only for records created in the current run. → Add a small helper in the Testify view-model logic to perform rollback DELETE against an entity instance URL, treating HTTP 2xx and HTTP 404 as success, and log rollback outcomes separately from normal cleanup. → Update the main Testify run flow so that if POST succeeded in the current run and any later PATCH or CE-verification step throws, the helper is invoked before the failure is finalized. → Clear `LastEntityInstanceUrl` and `LastRunToken` on the in-memory configuration after a successful rollback, then persist that cleared state through `TestifyConfigurationStore` so stale idempotency data is not reused on the next run. → Preserve existing idempotent reuse behavior by ensuring rollback is skipped for reused records from prior runs; only records freshly created during the current execution should be auto-deleted on failure.","- Risks: Rollback could accidentally delete a reused record from a prior run if the implementation does not clearly track whether the current execution created the entity.; Clearing configuration state only in memory without persisting it would leave `LastEntityInstanceUrl` stale across app restarts.; DELETE 404 handling must be limited to rollback/cleanup semantics; broadening it carelessly could hide genuine failures in other write paths.","- Suggested validation: dotnet test tests/FoToolbox.Tests/FoToolbox.Tests.csproj --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~Testify\""],"taskContext":["- Backlog counts: todo 4, in_progress 1, blocked 0, done 1","- Next actionable task: T2 (in_progress)","- Selected task id: T2","- Title: Testify automatic rollback on failure","- Status: in_progress","- Parent task: none","- Dependencies: T1 (done)","- Direct children: none","- Remaining descendants: none","- Task validation hint: dotnet test .\\FoToolbox.sln -c Release --filter Category=Testify","- Effective validation command: dotnet test .\\FoToolbox.sln -c Release --filter Category=Testify","- Validation command normalized from: none","- Notes: none","- Blocker: none","- Acceptance criteria: (1) If PATCH or CE-verification fails after a successful POST, the created record is deleted automatically (2) lastEntityInstanceUrl is cleared from TestifyConfigurationStore after rollback (3) Cleanup phase returns success (no error) when a cached URL references a record already deleted externally","- Constraints: none","- Relevant files: plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/TestifyRunner.cs, plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/DualWriteMapBrowserViewModel.Testify.cs, plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/TestifyConfigurationStore.cs","- Task-local code context: plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/TestifyRunner.cs, plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/DualWriteMapBrowserViewModel.Testify.cs, plugins/DualWriteMapBrowser/TestifyConfigurationStore.cs"],"progressContext":["- Ralph workspace initialized.","- Us